IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part I (Monthly Pension): THE NOUNS of piece oa1 that more than one module shares.
--
-- This module holds DECLAREs and nothing else. It states no rule of law; the rules that read these records
-- are in the oa1-part1-* modules. The core (oas-core*) declares what the whole text shares; these are the
-- records that only Part I reads. Every name carries the label of the provision it serves.
--
-- Conventions (the keel's, see NOTES.md): a period of residence or absence is a NUMBER of years, a fraction of a
-- year being a fraction; a date is a DATE; "the day on which the person's application is approved" is a DATE
-- the person (or the Minister's notice to them) states. Every fact here is one the person can state.

-- The facts that sections 3(1) and 3(2) read. Each is tested at the time the Act words it: on July 1, 1977, or on
-- the day on which the person's application is approved, or on the day preceding that day (fork OA1-F1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:95 | Payment of full pension
-- src:96 | 3 (1) Subject to this Act and the regulations, a full monthly pension may be paid to
-- src:97 | (a) every person who was a pensioner on July 1, 1977;
-- src:98 | (b) every person who
-- src:99 | (i) on July 1, 1977 was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and resided in Canada or, if that person did not reside in Canada, had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age or possessed a valid immigration visa,
-- src:100 | (ii) has attained sixty-five years of age, and
-- src:101 | (iii) has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved or, if that person has not so resided, has, after attaining eighteen years of age, been present in Canada prior to those ten years for an aggregate period at least equal to three times the aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years, and has resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved; and
-- src:102 | (c) every person who
-- src:103 | (i) was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977,
-- src:104 | (ii) has attained sixty-five years of age, and
-- src:105 | (iii) has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved for an aggregate period of at least forty years.
-- src:106 | Payment of partial pension
-- src:107 | (2) Subject to this Act and the regulations, a partial monthly pension may be paid for any month in a payment quarter to every person who is not eligible for a full monthly pension under subsection (1) and
-- src:108 | (a) has attained sixty-five years of age; and
-- src:109 | (b) has resided in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which that person’s application is approved for an aggregate period of at least ten years but less than forty years and, where that aggregate period is less than twenty years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 3(1), 3(2) (src:95-109)
DECLARE `s 3: Facts of age and residence` HAS
    -- the person's date of birth (needed for "has attained sixty-five years of age" and "had attained twenty-five years of age")
    `the date of birth` IS A DATE
    -- the day on which the person's application is approved (the Act tests the residence periods "prior to" it)
    `the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A DATE
    -- "was a pensioner on July 1, 1977": an application for a pension had been approved by then (s 2 "pensioner")
    -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "pensioner", the keel's definition
    `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1)(b)(i): the 1977 facts
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): Regulations, "resides in Canada", "present in Canada"
    `resided in Canada on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had resided in Canada for any period after attaining eighteen years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `possessed a valid immigration visa on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1)(b)(iii): the ten years immediately preceding the day of approval
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): as above
    `resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- years, after attaining eighteen, present in Canada prior to those ten years
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): as above
    `aggregate period of presence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age, prior to those ten years` IS A NUMBER
    -- years of absence from Canada during those ten years
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): as above
    `aggregate periods of absence from Canada during those ten years` IS A NUMBER
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): as above
    `resided in Canada for at least one year immediately preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 3(1)(c)(iii) and 3(2)(b): years resided in Canada after attaining eighteen and prior to the day of approval
    -- out of range: section 21 (piece oa3): as above
    `aggregate period of residence in Canada after attaining eighteen years of age and prior to the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A NUMBER
    `was resident in Canada on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts that section 4(1) reads: status on the day preceding the day of approval, and on the day preceding the
-- day the person ceased to reside in Canada. "Legally resident" is explained by Regulations s 22(1), which piece oa3
-- encodes: the person states whether they were.
-- src:116 | Residence in Canada must be or have been legal
-- src:117 | 4 (1) A person who was not a pensioner on July 1, 1977 is eligible for a pension under this Part only if
-- src:118 | (a) on the day preceding the day on which that person’s application is approved that person is a Canadian citizen or, if not, is legally resident in Canada; or
-- src:119 | (b) on the day preceding the day that person ceased to reside in Canada that person was a Canadian citizen or, if not, was legally resident in Canada.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 4(1) (src:116-119)
DECLARE `s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` HAS
    -- out of range: section 2 (piece oas-g0): "pensioner", the keel's definition
    `the person's application for a pension had been approved on July 1, 1977` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: section 22(1) (piece oa3): Regulations, "legally resident"
    `on the day preceding the day on which the person's application is approved, the person is legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has ceased to reside in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- out of range: section 22(1) (piece oa3): Regulations, "legally resident"
    `on the day preceding the day the person ceased to reside in Canada, the person was legally resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
